Loom: place loop-carried storage frames together. Values joined by same-storage relations (copies, slices, concats,
edges) share a frame with fixed unit offsets; once a member is placed, free-location search prefers the location it
predicts for the others, and a frame's first member starts at an aligned span that fits the whole frame. Loop header
arguments with a predicted frame are assigned first at their acquisition point. Lane-decomposed accumulators (WMMA
results sliced into a loop's block arguments) then keep one location around the backedge instead of copying every
lane (gen_gdn_ss: row loop backedge 100 -> 33 v_mov).
